WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.420
The way we validate products,

00:00:01.421 --> 00:00:02.341
let's say, okay,

00:00:02.342 --> 00:00:02.741
have this, like,

00:00:02.742 --> 00:00:04.021
crazy idea. We want to test,

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:04.861
like, a new product.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:07.661
What we do is to just validate that demand. Initially,

00:00:07.662 --> 00:00:09.501
we're just ordering the product from Amazon,

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:09.821
like, 2,

00:00:09.822 --> 00:00:10.421
3 days, boom,

00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:12.341
it's delivered. We slapping our logo on it.

00:00:12.342 --> 00:00:13.061
We're just printing, like,

00:00:13.062 --> 00:00:14.261
a sticker. Boom, done.

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:15.741
We're shooting some content with it.

00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:18.341
We just running a semester to validate the product.

00:00:18.342 --> 00:00:20.581
You move fast. You don't have to have the product in stock.

00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:21.181
You know that. Like,

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:23.541
if the product sells and if the margin makes sense,

00:00:23.542 --> 00:00:24.581
then you'll be able to source.

00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:25.421
The biggest part is, like,

00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:26.541
actually validating it.

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:28.981
One of the reasons why taking content from TikTok

00:00:28.982 --> 00:00:30.301
and passing it on Facebook,

00:00:30.302 --> 00:00:30.861
it didn't work,

00:00:30.862 --> 00:00:34.501
it could be because of Facebook has very good content detection system.

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:36.701
So if they see that the content is stolen,

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.421
they detect it. They kind of suppress the traffic for it.

00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:42.609
So Facebook really appreciates the uniqueness of the content.
